<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Collegiata, San Gimignano</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Collegiata di Santa Maria Assunta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Collegiata is the main church of San Gimignano in Tuscany, consecrated in 1148. Its interior is covered with 14th-century frescoes of the Old and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-testament">New Testaments</a> by Sienese painters, including Bartolo di Fredi, and its Santa Fina chapel was frescoed by Domenico Ghirlandaio. It is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> of the town.</p></div>
